WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:12.190
Hey Thoughty2 here, let's take a look at what's
going on in Syria.

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:17.040
Many north African and middle eastern countries
are ruled by an iron fist; governments that

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:22.650
pretend to be democracies but display strong
dictatorship qualities and oppress change.

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:27.940
In recent years there has been a sudden influx
of mass demonstrations in these arab countries,

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:30.590
attempting to overthrow their corrupt rulers.

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:36.580
It's called the "Arab Spring" and it was all
started in Tunisia in 2010, by a single fruit

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:42.150
and vegetable seller named Mohamed Bouazizi
after he set himself on fire in protest of

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:43.150
the government.

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:48.510
The Tunisian Revolution subsequently inspired
other Arab nations across North Africa and

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:51.600
the Middle East to protest, notably Egypt.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:55.070
Syria is the latest to jump on the revolutionary
bandwagon.

00:00:55.070 --> 00:01:00.199
Syria has been ruled by the same Syrian family,
the Assads, since 1971.

00:01:00.199 --> 00:01:02.860
Their political party is the Ba'ath party.

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:07.689
The current Syrian President Bashar al-Assad
has been in power since 2000.

00:01:07.689 --> 00:01:14.720
In the last referendum, in 2007, Bashar al-Assad
was the only candidate, securing his presidency

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:16.650
for another seven year term.

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:17.690
Seems fair.

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:24.110
Sick of the Assad's tight regime, on the 15th
March 2011, Syrian civilians started their

00:01:24.110 --> 00:01:29.500
own Arab Spring protest, which quickly gained
momentum and evolved into the Syrian civil

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:30.500
war.

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:36.659
In July 2011 the Free Syrian Army was formed,
an umbrella group representing the Syrian

00:01:36.659 --> 00:01:37.659
rebels.

00:01:37.659 --> 00:01:43.870
In April 2011 the Syrian Government's Army
was deployed to stop the uprising in its tracks.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:48.070
Soldiers fired on demonstrators in towns and
cities across the country.

00:01:48.070 --> 00:01:52.700
After months of military siege the protestors
got their hands on weapons of their own and

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:59.450
started a full scale armed rebellion consisting
of defected soldiers and civilian volunteers.

00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:05.340
Syrian Allies Russia and Iran supply the government
with weapons, whilst Qatar and Saudi Arabia

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:07.550
provide the rebels with their weaponry.

00:02:07.550 --> 00:02:13.390
The death toll has now surpassed 100,000,
half of which are civilians, including both

00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:15.910
rebels and innocent bystanders.

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:20.500
The other half are Syrian Army soldiers and
1,000 government officials.

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:24.950
1.8 Million Syrians have fled the country
to escape the violence.

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:29.150
Tens of thousands of protestors have been
imprisoned and there are widespread reports

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:31.230
of torture in the nation's prisons.

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:36.670
The Syrian government and protestors have
both been accused of severe human rights abuse.

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:41.421
However the United Nation's investigations
have concluded that the Syrian government's

00:02:41.421 --> 00:02:44.310
human rights abuse has been far greater.

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:47.310
But the rebel's aren't exactly saints either.

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:53.740
Certain Syrian rebel groups have pledged loyalty
to al-Qaeda and beheaded numerous Christians.

00:02:53.740 --> 00:03:00.099
In January 2012 the Syrian army started to
use large-scale artillery and tanks against

00:03:00.099 --> 00:03:05.130
the rebel army which led to many civilian
homes being destroyed because of indiscriminate

00:03:05.130 --> 00:03:06.130
shelling.

00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:11.430
By July 2012 the fighting had spread across
the whole country and the International Committee

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:14.790
of the Red Cross declared the conflict a civil
war.

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:18.709
The fighting focussed on Syria's capital city,
Damascus.

00:03:18.709 --> 00:03:23.940
By late July the government managed to push
back the rebel forces in Damascus and the

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:26.960
focus of the war shifted to the city Aleppo.

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:32.349
A year later and the bulk of the Syrian civil
war still revolves around Aleppo.

00:03:32.349 --> 00:03:35.380
So what's the latest news on the Syria convict?

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:40.550
The rebels and Western governments have accused
the Syrian government of using chemical weapons

00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:49.540
in attacks that killed more than 1,429 people
near Damascus, 426 of which were children.

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:52.500
One of the bombs was dropped onto a school
playground.

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:56.459
The use of chemical weapons is strictly outlawed
by international law.

00:03:56.459 --> 00:04:00.599
The Syrian government have said the rebels
were behind the chemical attacks, however

00:04:00.599 --> 00:04:05.120
according to the US government, the rockets
were only launched from government controlled

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:09.120
areas and only aimed towards opposition controlled
areas.

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:13.870
On the 30th August British prime minister
David Cameron was defeated in the House of

00:04:13.870 --> 00:04:19.269
Commons in a vote to join the US in strikes
against Syria, in order to deter the use of

00:04:19.269 --> 00:04:20.600
chemical weapons.

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:24.870
Therefore Britain will not be involved in
any military action in Syria.

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:29.279
The US is a bit miffed with this decision
but they have said they will continue to consult

00:04:29.279 --> 00:04:32.370
with the UK, one of their closest allies.

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:37.379
Obama has said the US will be responding to
the use of chemical weapons in Syria, but

00:04:37.379 --> 00:04:41.360
he stated there will be no "boots on the ground".

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:43.310
In other words...

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:48.069
Many skeptics are against the use of military
action in Syria, fearing it may be a repeat

00:04:48.069 --> 00:04:49.069
of Iraq.

00:04:49.069 --> 00:04:54.300
60% of the United States public says the US
government should not take military action

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:55.330
against Syria.

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:58.860
Many fear such an attack could lead to World
War 3.

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:05.419
Syria has said it will use "all means available"
to defend itself if the United States attacks.

00:05:05.419 --> 00:05:08.900
Which could include terror attacks in the
US itself.

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:13.119
Russia have sent their most advanced anti-ship
missiles to Syria.

00:05:13.119 --> 00:05:17.789
If one of those sinks a US vessel it would
be sure to escalate matters to a whole new

00:05:17.789 --> 00:05:18.789
level.

00:05:18.789 --> 00:05:23.449
There is a very good chance that if the US
attacks Syria, Syria will attack Israel.

00:05:23.449 --> 00:05:29.619
Israel have said it would respond to any attack
"forcefully", which would surely spell disaster.

00:05:29.619 --> 00:05:35.849
Iran's closest ally is Syria and Iran aren't
going to take an attack against Syria lightly.

00:05:35.849 --> 00:05:41.150
Furthermore an attack against Syria will seriously
damage the United State's relationship with

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:42.150
Russia.

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:46.880
All of these factors and many more could easily
contribute to the start of the next World

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:47.880
War.

